FL,304,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30304
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786681089
OL,3,CMore than 60% of adults have not
OL,4,Cbought sunscreen so far this year `
OL,5,Csurvey
OL,7,FCancer information nurse at Cancer
OL,8,FResearch UK, Caroline Geraghty, said:
OL,9,F"With temperatures skyrocketing across
OL,10,Fthe UK this summer, it's easy to focus
OL,11,Fon the heat and forget about UV.
OL,13,F"But it's UV radiation, not
OL,14,Ftemperature, that causes sun damage.
OL,16,F"Sunscreen isn't a suit of armour.
OL,17,FSeeking shade and covering up with
OL,18,Fclothing are some of the most
OL,19,Feffective and affordable ways to
OL,20,Fprotect yourself from the sun's
OL,21,Fharmful rays.
OL,26,@qD@AOUuD@AOUxD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30305
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786681089
OL,3,CMore than 60% of adults have not
OL,4,Cbought sunscreen so far this year `
OL,5,Csurvey
OL,7,F"Checking the UV index on your weather
OL,8,Fapp can help you plan ahead and know
OL,9,Fwhen it's time to take extra
OL,10,Fprecautions."
OL,12,FMelanoma skin cancer is the fifth most
OL,13,Fcommon cancer in the UK, with almost
OL,14,Fnine in 10 melanoma skin cancer cases
OL,15,Fcaused by excess ultraviolet (UV)
OL,16,Fexposure.
OL,26,@oD@AOUrD@MO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/7
